{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/564570-deceived-blessed-is-the-god-king-and-sekhem-drain","id":564570,"title":"Deceived, Blessed Is The God-King, and Sekhem Drain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-22T14:40:26-07:00","id":564570,"title":"Deceived, Blessed Is The God-King, and Sekhem Drain","content":"So, the Deceived version of Blessed Is The God-King states that the user's Sekhem and Willpower rises to 10 and remains so while the form lasts. How do you think this would react to the efforts of Amkhata and Shuankhsen to drain the user's Sekhem? Should the clause &quot;and remains so&quot; preclude any possibility of losing Sekhem? If not, and the Deceived does suffer a loss of Sekhem, does it only affect the temporary Sekhem he has by virtue of the Utterance (dropping him to 9 until the end of the Utterance, but leaving his permanent rating the same)? Or, when he returns to his normal Sekhem rating, would he be one less than he was before unleashing the Utterance?<br /> <br /> I'm leaning in favour of an immunity to Sekhem drain, but it sees like a fairly considerable benefit to add to the various bonuses already granted by the unleashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:06:08-07:00","id":564606,"title":"","content":"The Sekhem and Willpower rise is not new to the Deceived.<br /> <br /> I...hmm, good questions. I'd say THey'd devour the normal level of Sekhem, but while the power is going the Deceived/Arisen is still at 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T16:24:57-07:00","id":564727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/564570-deceived-blessed-is-the-god-king-and-sekhem-drain#post564570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Deceived version of Blessed Is The God-King states that the user's Sekhem and Willpower rises to 10 and remains so while the form lasts. How do you think this would react to the efforts of Amkhata and Shuankhsen to drain the user's Sekhem?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deceived version of BITGK is not showing the Arisen's soul but rather showing the full force of a embodied Shan'iatu through the Temakh. It is effectively a God/Demigod walking.<br /> <br /> I would allow the drain but not allow it to drop. You're facing the full fury of a walking god back in it's prime and is one of the many reasons why you do not piss off the Deceived. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:31:50-07:00","id":564809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/564570-deceived-blessed-is-the-god-king-and-sekhem-drain?p=564606#post564606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sekhem and Willpower rise is not new to the Deceived.<br /> <br /> I...hmm, good questions. I'd say THey'd devour the normal level of Sekhem, but while the power is going the Deceived/Arisen is still at 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a decent compromise. Thank you.<br /> <br /> The Sekhem/Willpower rise is actually new to Deceived though. There are other powers that replicate the Sekhem rise to which this question would be pertinent, I guess (Entombed Glory, perhaps?) but the Arisen version of Blessed Is The God-King just allows the Arisen to spend Pillars on Attributes as if they were Sekhem 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T19:39:51-07:00","id":565979,"title":"","content":"Makes one shudder to think of what the Shan'iatu were capable of in their prime, considering how much power the Temakh of the Deceived can bring to bear, even in their degraded and broken state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}